WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:02.720
Hey Brian, you're back from vacation, huh?

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:04.080
So I heard a lot about these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:07.600
Squidward Games, and I have to write something&nbsp;
about it. Can you fill me in?

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:12.160
Can I! So, you’ve got this guy&nbsp;
Gi-hun. He's kind of your average,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:15.760
everyday dirtbag who gives his&nbsp;
daughter a gun for her tenth birthday.

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:17.120
Wait, what? A gun?

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:21.200
Relax: it's just for lighting cigarettes!&nbsp;
So he's deep in debt with loan sharks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.560
but then one day an angel comes&nbsp;
along and throws him a lifeline.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:25.440
Sounds uplifting!

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:27.760
It is! You ever play pogs when you were a kid?

00:00:27.935 --> 00:00:29.120
Pogs, yeah I played it!

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:32.080
Okay, so you know the rules: Somebody&nbsp;
gives you eight dollars every time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:34.800
you win. And if you lose, they&nbsp;
get to slap you in the face.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:36.640
What?

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:37.520
Slap-pogs!

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.240
Is he good at Slap-Pogs?

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:45.840
He's not great. So naturally after he gets slapped&nbsp;
for several hours and finally wins eight dollars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:49.840
he does what any of us would do: He gives&nbsp;
himself over to a mysterious organization,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:53.280
allows himself to be kidnapped and drugged,&nbsp;
and says yes to literally anything.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.320
Sort of like that week I&nbsp;
spent at the Improv Olympics.

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:57.040
Yes, and?

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:00.480
So anyway, there's a lot of colorful&nbsp;
characters playing these Squid Games.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:01.680
Like who, for example?

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:04.800
Well, you’ve got Gi-hun, of&nbsp;
course. You got Gi-hun’s mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:09.040
smart friend with the glasses. You got old&nbsp;
Snake Face, who's got the snakiest face&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:13.920
of the whole lot of 'em. You’ve got Crazy Toilet Lady and&nbsp;
her maybe imaginary kids. You’ve got Stabby,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:17.440
who’ll stab her way out of anything&nbsp;
if you give her a sharp object, or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:24.640
even a blunt one. And, of course, you’ve got&nbsp;
A Harmless Old Man Who Isn’t Hiding Anything.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:29.280
I like the sound of that last guy!&nbsp;
So what sorts of games do they play?

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:31.920
Well, do you remember playing&nbsp;
“Red Light, Green Light” as a kid?

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:34.320
Yes! But not with any slapping.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:35.360
Brian!

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:39.520
Don't worry, red light green light is a slap-free zone.

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:40.320
Okay, cool.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:45.360
Instead, when the big robot lady turns her head&nbsp;
around and she says red light and you so much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:51.120
as move an eyebrow the wrong way, a sniper rifle&nbsp;
blows half your head clean off! It's super fun.

00:01:52.896 --> 00:01:54.080
What?

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:57.200
It’s partly to illustrate just how&nbsp;
brutal this whole squid game is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:01.120
and partly to cut down on background&nbsp;
extras in your pilot episode so your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:04.720
craft services budget doesn’t spiral out of control. Anyway,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:09.040
after that, everyone leaves the game because&nbsp;
they realize it’s a brutal exercise in futility.

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:09.760
Oh, thank God.

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:13.680
But right after that, they all figure&nbsp;
out they live horrible garbage lives,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:16.400
so they just join the game again, and it takes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:20.400
forty-five entire minutes of on-screen&nbsp;
misery for everyone to get to that point.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:21.920
Oh. Cool.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:25.040
So, we've already established you’re&nbsp;
familiar with “Red Light, Green Light.”

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:26.640
Right, not that version, but-

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:29.440
Well, they play a lot of other&nbsp;
classic childhood games too!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:33.520
This Squid Game has everything: Tug Of&nbsp;
War, Carve Sugar Good Or You’ll Die,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:38.240
Murder Marbles, Exploding Glass Bridge, Do&nbsp;
All Of The Stabbing Before Anybody Else Can…

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:38.960
Monopoly?

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:40.800
Be serious, man. They’re not total monsters.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:42.560
So the players fall one-by-one:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:49.200
Snake Face, Crazy Toilet Lady, A Harmless&nbsp;
Old Man Who Isn't Hiding Anything, Stabby. Stabby dies.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.920
Oh no, not Stabby. How does she die?

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:55.040
It's kind of a great twist. She gets stabbed.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:58.400
Sure. She who lives by the stab&nbsp;
must also die by the stab. I guess.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:02:59.680
This is so bad.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:00.868
Uh-huh.

00:03:00.868 --> 00:03:02.383
This is the absolute worst.

00:03:02.383 --> 00:03:03.040
Yeah mhm.

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:04.800
Can you believe how awful this is?

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:05.920
Not really.

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:09.120
Who would ever want to actually watch&nbsp;
this, let alone pay money for it?

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.880
Wait, I thought you liked this?

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:13.920
Oh, I loved it! Those are the&nbsp;
names of episodes 4 through 7.

00:03:15.234 --> 00:03:16.240
wakka wakka

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:21.200
So that takes us to our titular Squid Game. There&nbsp;
are two players left. Gi-Hun, and his mean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:25.920
friend with glasses. Only — and here's another&nbsp;
great twist — he ain't got his glasses no more.

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:27.120
What happened to his glasses?

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:30.880
Who gives a s---, Brian? I'M TRYING&nbsp;
TO TELL YOU ABOUT THE SQUID GAME!

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:32.880
Okay! So, what is the Squid Game?

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:36.400
Well it's this game where they run around&nbsp;
for some reason, sometimes on one foot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:39.680
sometimes on two foots, on a&nbsp;
court that's shaped like a squid.

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:41.200
Shaped like a squid?

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:45.840
Yeah! You know, a triangle, a circle, oh, let's not forget a square.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:48.160
I don't…

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:51.840
A squid! You know, like when you were&nbsp;
a kid, you used to live in a squid with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:54.800
your parents until they kicked you out&nbsp;
for what kept happening in the bathroom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.840
so now you and three other&nbsp;
dudes share a studio angelfish?

00:03:58.480 --> 00:03:59.280
I’m hanging up.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:00.880
I’ll give you eight bucks to keep listening

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.560
Go on.

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:04.480
So Gi-Hun wins, his buddy dies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:09.040
and the Squidwards set him free and pay&nbsp;
him the billions he's earned by not dying.

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:10.080
What about that old man?

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:11.520
Which one?

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:13.520
The innocent old man who isn’t hiding anything?

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:16.560
Oh! It turns out that those were HIS squid games!

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:19.680
Sure. Wait, so they pay Gi-Hun the money?

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:20.400
Yeah.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:21.680
Why don’t they just kill him?

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:22.180
I dunno.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:25.440
Why don’t they dump him on&nbsp;
the street and then not pay him?

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:25.940
I dunno.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:30.240
It’s just that it seems like this whole&nbsp;
thing is an unnecessarily long buildup to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:33.680
a shaky conclusion that doesn't hold up to&nbsp;
even a single second of narrative scrutiny.

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:35.600
He wears a funny red wig at the end!

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:37.760
I'm just really confused about —

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:41.760
Listen, friend. It’s not the plot that matters&nbsp;
so much as the message. The message is that if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:47.840
you gamble and lose and gamble and lose and gamble&nbsp;
and lose and gamble and lose and then you gamble&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:53.120
and then you lose and your wife leaves you because&nbsp;
you gamble and lose so much and then you gamble&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:59.040
and then you lose again and then someone says&nbsp;
“would you like to gamble,” there’s a pretty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:09.840
good chance that you’re going to be okay. Maybe.&nbsp;
Or you’ll die! It’s one of those. Brian? Brian?

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:13.200
Bri-Bri?

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:17.120
Guess I get to keep my eight bucks.

